course: dictionary
lesson: 6252
title: Moisten: making things a little wet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Moisten is a verb, so it describes an action. It means to make something slightly wet, or to become slightly wet. The key word is slightly: a moistened cloth is damp, not dripping. «Moisten the cloth» tells you to add a little water, not a lot.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «The nose warms and moistens air, and its hairs and sticky mucus catch dust and germs before they reach the lungs.» Warms and catch dust tell you the nose is doing useful work on the air. Moistens must mean it makes the air a little damp before it reaches the lungs.
explain: The same word can work on people too. «Her eyes moistened» means her eyes became slightly wet, with tears starting to form. The sentence does not say she is crying hard. It shows she is close to tears. Ask yourself: what would the sentence look like if I put in a similar word, such as dampen? If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Moisten is a verb: moisten, moistens, moistened, moistening.
fact: To moisten something means to make it slightly wet.
fact: «Moisten the flour with a little water» means add only a small amount of water.
fact: «The nose warms and moistens air» means the nose makes the air a little damp.
fact: «Her eyes moistened» shows a character is close to tears.

exercise: «Moisten the flour with a little water before you add the eggs.» What does moisten mean here? | To cut into small pieces | To make something very hot | To mix with sugar | *To make something slightly wet
exercise: «The nose warms and moistens air, and its hairs and sticky mucus catch dust and germs.» Find and copy the word that means make slightly wet. | warms | catch | germs | *moistens
exercise: «Her eyes moistened as she read the letter.» What does this show? | *She was close to tears | She was very cold | She was laughing loudly | She was falling asleep
test: Seeds need moistened soil to germinate. What does moistened mean here? | Dried out | Frozen hard | Covered in sand | *Slightly wet
test: «Moisten the cloth» means which of these? Choose the best swap. | Shout | Crumble | *Dampen | Freeze
exam: A recipe says «moisten the flour». What should you do? | Freeze it solid | Dig a hole in it | *Add a little water until it is slightly wet | Throw it away
